# wave 52: no Drupal 11 compatible release on drupal.org (max core ^10)
# wave 52: has D11 releases but unresolvable on this site
# twig: no drupal/twig package on packagist
# external_entities: needs galbar/jsonpath ^2|^3, subrequests pins ^1.0
# apigee_edge: apigee-client-php needs firebase/php-jwt ^7.0, conflicts
# ckeditor_resize: D11 release depends on drupal/ckeditor (core <=^10)
# acquia_cms_tour: acquia_cms_common caps at core <10.0.9
# user_revision: newest release still core ^9 || ^10
# advanced_search: needs facets ^2.0, root has facets 3.x
# controlled_access_terms: needs geolocation ^3.2 / auto_entitylabel ^2.1, both conflict
# smart_date_calendar_kit: needs add_content_by_bundle ^1.0, conflicts
# sendgrid_api: sendgrid/sendgrid vs locked sendgrid_integration/fastglass
# already documented under their module machine name (project->module rename)
# wave 52 scan: no Drupal 11 compatible release on drupal.org (checked 2026-08-05)
# already documented under their module machine name (project->module rename)
# on disk but no D11-compatible release installed
# documented under their module machine name (project -> module rename), wave 53
# wave 54 scan: no Drupal 11 compatible release on drupal.org (checked 2026-08-05)
# corrected packagist-metadata scan: no release allows drupal/core ^11
# state_log 2.3.0: StateLog does not implement StateInterface::getValuesSetDuringRequest,
# and state_logger forms a circular service reference. Its mere presence on disk fatals the
# container on Drupal 11.4, taking down every later drush call in the wave (wave 58).
# bat_api 11.1.0-rc3 pulls in drupal/bat, whose BatEventHandlerBlockingFilter declares
# $value_value protected where the parent Views BooleanOperator declares it public. PHP fatals
# on Views plugin discovery, breaking the whole site (wave 60).
# rest_entity_recursive 2.0.6-rc8: ReferenceItemNormalizer::normalize() declares a return type
# incompatible with the parent EntityReferenceFieldItemNormalizer::normalize(), which fatals PHP on
# every request once the module is on disk (wave 67).
# bee (Bee) requires bat, which is already skip-listed: BatEventHandlerBlockingFilter
# declares $value_value protected where core's BooleanOperator declares it public, so the
# mere presence of bat on disk fatals plugin discovery and takes down every drush call.
# bee installs and enables, then breaks the site the moment views plugins are rebuilt (wave 73).
# wave 84: wisski 8.x-4.3 - wisski.route_subscriber requires search.search_page_repository
# but wisski/wisski_core do not declare core search as a dependency, so enabling it
# breaks container compilation and takes drush down with it (verified). Also leaves
# wisski_title_n_grams unqueryable after a partial install. Document from source.
# wave 84: composer reported no Drupal 11 release despite check-d11.sh passing
# (the packagist metadata heuristic and composer's resolver disagree for these).
# wave 84: vardot/varbase-patches no longer applies to the current release of a
# package it targets (drupal/embed, entity_embed, ckeditor_media_resize).
# wave 84: drupal/webform_bootstrap is a METAPACKAGE that installs drupal/webform;
# the module ships at webform/modules/webform_bootstrap and is documented there.
# wave 84: project imce_search_2 ships module imce_search_plugin, documented under
# that name; next-wave.sh cannot see the rename.
# wave 85: bs_lib 8.x-1.0-rc3 - BsLibCommands::__construct() calls
# $theme_handler->getTheme('bs_base') unconditionally, and ThemeHandler::getTheme()
# THROWS when the theme is not installed. Drush instantiates every drush.command-tagged
# service at bootstrap, so enabling bs_lib kills the ENTIRE drush CLI for the site
# ("The theme bs_base does not exist.") while the website keeps serving 200s. drush
# pm:uninstall bs_lib cannot run either; recovery needs a direct core.extension DB edit.
# bs_lib.info.yml declares no dependencies and a module cannot enforce a theme dependency.
# wave 85: composer could not resolve these.
# varbase_blog - vardot/varbase-patches no longer applies to a current dependency release.
# instagram_feeds, mysql56 - no Drupal 11 release despite check-d11.sh passing.
# wave 85: lb_branch_hours_blocks constrains ycloudyusa/y_lb ^4 || ^5, but Packagist only
# publishes y_lb 0.1 (2022). The current y_lb lives in the YMCA's own composer repository,
# which this campaign does not add. Documented from source alongside its siblings.
# wave 85: project entity_meta_relation ships module `emr`, documented under modules/em/emr.
# next-wave.sh cannot see the rename.
# wave 86: apigee_m10n pulls apigee_edge 4.1.0, whose services inject the container parameter
# %main_content_renderers% into EdgeExceptionSubscriber and TeamInactiveStatusSubscriber.
# Drupal 11.4 core NO LONGER DEFINES that parameter, so the container fails to compile:
# "DefinitionErrorExceptionPass: You have requested a non-existent parameter
# main_content_renderers". Site and drush both down; it fataled mid-wave and left 80 of 120
# modules half-installed. Documented from source.
# wave 86: no Drupal 11 release despite check-d11.sh passing.
# wave 87: the YMCA Layout Builder family again — these require ycloudyusa/y_lb ^3/^4/^5,
# and Packagist publishes only y_lb 0.1 (2022, core ^8 || ^9). The current y_lb lives in the
# YMCA's own composer repository, which this campaign does not add. Same root cause as
# lb_branch_hours_blocks (wave 85); see modules/y_/y_lb for the characterisation.
# wave 87: aws_cloudwatchlogs 8.x-1.2 carries a LATENT circular service dependency. Its
# aws_cloudwatchlogs.log is tagged { name: logger } — so it is collected into logger.factory —
# while depending on aws_cloudwatchlogs.put_log_events, which takes @logger.channel.aws_cloudwatchlogs,
# a channel obtained FROM logger.factory. Core's factory resolves channels lazily so the cycle
# never materialises alone; any module that DECORATES logger.factory surfaces it. flowdrop_runtime
# does exactly that, and the two together produce
# "ServiceCircularReferenceException: Circular reference detected for service
# flowdrop_runtime.logger_channel_filter" — container down, site and drush both. Documented from
# source; the module to fix is aws_cloudwatchlogs, not the decorator.
# wave 87: the canvas family cannot be enabled on this install.
# canvas_override 1.0.0-beta1 extends Drupal\canvas\Storage\ComponentTreeLoader, which canvas
# 1.8.0 declares FINAL — "cannot extend final class", fatal on class load. And canvas itself
# still trips assert($property !== NULL) in JsonSchemaPropsComponentSourceBase over third-party
# SDC components (characterised in wave 85), which with zend.assertions on is a container-build
# fatal. Both documented from source; the canvas assertion recurs whenever canvas meets SDC
# components from other modules, so it is not specific to one wave's module set.
# wave 88: the whole YMCA Layout Builder family is gated on ycloudyusa/y_lb ^4.0 || ^5.0, which
# Packagist cannot satisfy — it publishes only y_lb 0.1 (2022, core ^8 || ^9). Checked each of
# these against packages.drupal.org before installing: all ten require ^4.0 || ^5.0, so all ten
# would fail at composer time. Skip-listed up front rather than burning resolution on each.
#
# DECISION POINT, deliberately not taken here: adding the YMCA's own composer repository would
# unlock the entire family in one change, the same way asset-packagist unlocked npm-asset in
# wave 87. That is a supply-chain decision — a new third-party repository in the campaign
# environment — and it is the site owner's to make, not one to take unilaterally mid-campaign.
# If it is taken, remove these entries and the wave 85/87 y_lb entries together.
# YMCA Layout Builder family: requires ycloudyusa/y_lb, not on Packagist. See lb_hero/lb_table etc.
